+# Zhengzhou
+
+## Telemetry
+
+- Terrain: Located on the western edge of the Eastern Henan Plain along the south bank of the Yellow River, Zhengzhou rests against the foothills of the Songshan Mountains to the west and opens onto the Huanghuaihai alluvial plain to the east; its flat urban terrain descends gently from southwest to northeast.
+- Step: Located on China's third terrain step, at the eastern edge of the transition zone between the second and third steps, where the Qinling–Taihang mountain systems give way to the North China Plain.
+- Climate: Warm-temperate continental monsoon climate with four distinct seasons, hot rainy summers, and cold dry winters; representative urban elevation is about 110 metres.
+- Challenge: Midsummer heat and humidity with short, intense convective rainfall place sustained demands on vehicle cooling, energy management, equipment moisture protection, and crew hydration.
+
